```csharp
public RetryPolicyResult ShouldRetry(IRestResponse restResponse)
{
    if (restResponse == null)
        throw new ArgumentNullException("restResponse");

    bool shouldRetry = false;

    if (restResponse.ResponseStatus == ResponseStatus.Error)
    {
        // Re-resolve if the error type is one that cannot be fixed by retrying
        // the request on the same endpoint and instead requires resolving a new endpoint.
        shouldRetry =
            restResponse.ErrorException is ConnectionFailureException
            || restResponse.ErrorException is ReceiveFailureException
            || restResponse.ErrorException is SendFailureException
            || restResponse.ErrorException is ServiceResolutionTransientException
            || restResponse.ErrorException is ProtocolErrorException;
    }

    return new RetryPolicyResult(
        shouldRetry: shouldRetry,
        policyName: nameof(ResolverRetryPolicy),
        reason: $"Response Status: {restResponse.ResponseStatus}, Status Code: {restResponse.StatusCode}, Exception Type: {restResponse.ErrorException?.GetType().FullName ?? string.Empty}, Seen Authentication Failure: {this.seenAuthenticationFailure}");
}
```

**Key Point:** `ConnectionFailureException` triggers service endpoint **re-resolution** (not simple retry), indicating this is a transient infrastructure issue.

