### **C. FILE DELETE WITH RETRY - THROWS UnauthorizedAccessException**

**Location:** `CsvFileCache.cs`, lines 600-638
```csharp
private async Task RemoveFileAsync(string filePath, CancellationToken token)
{
    const int maxRetries = 5;
    const int retryDelayMs = 100;

    var fileLock = this.GetOrCreateFileLock(filePath);

    await fileLock.WaitAsync(token);
    try
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++)
        {
            try
            {
                File.Delete(filePath);

                if (!File.Exists(filePath))
                {
                    return;
                }
            }
            catch (IOException) when (i < maxRetries - 1)
            {
                // File might be in use, retry
            }
            catch (UnauthorizedAccessException) when (i < maxRetries - 1)  // LINE 625
            {
                // Access denied, retry
            }

            await Task.Delay(retryDelayMs * (i + 1), token);
        }
    }
    finally
    {
        fileLock.Release();
        this.CleanupFileLockIfPossible(filePath);
    }
}
```

**⚠️ CRITICAL:** `UnauthorizedAccessException` is caught **with retry logic**, but if it occurs **during service startup in RegisterCaching()**, there's NO retry mechanism at that level!

